{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/981878-how-long-is-too-long-time-to-be-stuck-in-the-umbra","id":981878,"title":"How long is \"Too Long\" time to be stuck in The Umbra?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-04T18:28:54-07:00","id":981878,"title":"How long is \"Too Long\" time to be stuck in The Umbra?","content":"So, my old ST told me that if a PC stays TOO LONG in any layer of the Umbra, he becomes a wandering spirit and he cant return to the Physical Plane... How long is that ammount of time?<br /> Does that rule also applies for the Umbral Realms?<br /> Any ways to tell how long you been there, like physical signs that aim to the point of no return ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:34:23-07:00","id":981887,"title":"","content":"I always figured it didn't screw with garou since they are already half spirit. In mage it's like 3 weeks or something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:54:19-07:00","id":981896,"title":"","content":"I don't think there are any guidelines in the books so I imagine it is up to the discretion of the ST. How long is too long for you (i.e. you don't want to run a game solely in the Umbra for that long)? Garou are creatures of both the Realm and the Umbra, so they are supposed to spend time in both. From what I see of most players, PCs spend over 90% of their time in the Realm and only enter the Umbra for tactical reasons. If that is good enough to keep them centered, then the opposite should also be true (a Garou who spends 90% of their time in the Umbra and enter the Realm rarely).<br /> <br /> I think the few Garou who become lost in the Umbra are the ones who spend all their time on vision quests exploring the Near Realms, the Deep Umbra, etc. If you are just farting about in the Penumbra, you are fine. Personally, I am thinking of months spent in the Umbra, perhaps even years, before a Garou becomes lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:45:28-07:00","id":981916,"title":"","content":"I have generally used a house rule of requiring Garou to spend one day in the Realm for every (Willpower) days in the Umbra and one day in the Umbra for every (Willpower) days in the Realm. If they violated that rule, they reduced their die pool to go to the other Realm by one per (Willpower) additional days spent on one side over the other. If their die pool reaches '0', they are temporarily Lost and become permanently Lost after (Willpower) months of being temporary Lost. Garou are supposed to be denizens of both the Realm and the Umbra, and they should not just use the Umbra as a tactical resource.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 10-04-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:15:04-07:00","id":981923,"title":"","content":"It's a psychological limit, not a physical one. You can spend years in the Legendary Realm, or Wolfhome, or Erebus, if you can keep your homid-mind and wolf-soul coherent. Once you start losing yourself, you risk becoming part of the realm you're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:37:14-07:00","id":981932,"title":"","content":"It's called Disconnection, p319 W20. Each lunar cycle in the Umbra adds one to the difficulty to return to the physical. Eventually it will become nearly impossible to escape. After a year and a day in the Umbra, shapeshifters become spirits.<br /> <br /> Homelands slow this dissolution for tribe members, adding 1 to the difficulty per year, rather than per month. Time is weird in the Deep Umbra, so Disconnection doesn't progress while in the Deep, but neither does any accumulated time reduce. This is all covered in W20 Umbra, p83 for Homelands and pp103-104 for Deep Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:33:49-07:00","id":981950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/981878-how-long-is-too-long-time-to-be-stuck-in-the-umbra?p=981932#post981932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called Disconnection, p319 W20. Each lunar cycle in the Umbra adds one to the difficulty to return to the physical. Eventually it will become nearly impossible to escape. After a year and a day in the Umbra, shapeshifters become spirits.<br /> <br /> Homelands slow this dissolution for tribe members, adding 1 to the difficulty per year, rather than per month. Time is weird in the Deep Umbra, so Disconnection doesn't progress while in the Deep, but neither does any accumulated time reduce. This is all covered in W20 Umbra, p83 for Homelands and pp103-104 for Deep Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they become like ancestor spirits or just spirits as we know them? Could they in theory become a pack totem? Iirc Fenris was originally garou wasn't he?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:32:35-07:00","id":982114,"title":"","content":"As different books of different lines affirm different rules<br /> so a thumb rule, I use this<br /> [Willpower] days + [Arete/Gnosis] weeks<br /> after that a Willpower (difficulty X) roll each month, if the roll is succesfull the disconnection is postponed to the next month.<br /> X is 5 in Near umbra, 6 in Middle Umbra and Dark Umbra (Shadowlands only), 7 in High Umbra or near-Earth umbral realm (Scar, Summer Country, Pangaea, the Battleground, the Tempest), 8 in Deep Umbra or far/alien umbral realm (Malfeas, Aetherial Realm, Labyrinth).<br /> Some realms slow or alt this process (homelands, stable mage realms, etc.).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:03:07-07:00","id":982379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/981878-how-long-is-too-long-time-to-be-stuck-in-the-umbra?p=981950#post981950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they become like ancestor spirits or just spirits as we know them? Could they in theory become a pack totem? Iirc Fenris was originally garou wasn't he?</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't rules for this, nor should there be. This is rare and something that should be governed on a case-by-case basis, I think. I like the idea of one becoming a lesser totem, though.<br /> <br /> One of my current plots involves an old Silent Strider Theurge seeking to become a powerful spirit; he is unwilling to undergo disconnection because it does not allow him to control what sort of spirit he becomes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:19:24-07:00","id":982426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/981878-how-long-is-too-long-time-to-be-stuck-in-the-umbra?p=981950#post981950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they become like ancestor spirits or just spirits as we know them? Could they in theory become a pack totem? Iirc Fenris was originally garou wasn't he?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes (ancestor spirits) and Yes (possible to become totems), I believe. I know there's also a Wyrm totem that used to be a a Shadow Lord. That said, I imagine it takes some additional spiritual umph or bargaining to get that kind of power. No packs that I know of are followers of Billy &quot;Two Left Shoes&quot; O'Malley, the Cliath Gnawer who got lost in the Umbra back in '89. We're probably talking about heroic elders and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Though maybe a devout follower of (Totem X) might join that totem's brood and become a pack totem spirit for later followers? If that's what you were getting at, that could make for a cool story.<br /> <br /> Edit: Page 10 of 2nd Edition Umbra: The Velvet Shadow is the part that specifies that Fera tend to turn into their respective ancestor spirits, as well as what happens to trapped mundanes. I've seen later publications generally hint at agreeing with this, but never seen the full splat on death/disconnection/starvation in the Umbra redone as fully hashed-out as the original block from 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":". 10-05-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:56:27-07:00","id":982495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/981878-how-long-is-too-long-time-to-be-stuck-in-the-umbra?p=982426#post982426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Edit: Page 10 of 2nd Edition Umbra: The Velvet Shadow is the part that specifies that Fera tend to turn into their respective ancestor spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>'Tend to' are important words here. If your story calls for lost shapeshifters to become something other than ancestor spirits, there's nothing stopping you from doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:26:44-07:00","id":982506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/981878-how-long-is-too-long-time-to-be-stuck-in-the-umbra?p=982426#post982426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes (ancestor spirits) and Yes (possible to become totems), I believe. I know there's also a Wyrm totem that used to be a a Shadow Lord. That said, I imagine it takes some additional spiritual umph or bargaining to get that kind of power. No packs that I know of are followers of Billy &amp;quot;Two Left Shoes&amp;quot; O'Malley, the Cliath Gnawer who got lost in the Umbra back in '89. We're probably talking about heroic elders and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Though maybe a devout follower of (Totem X) might join that totem's brood and become a pack totem spirit for later followers? If that's what you were getting at, that could make for a cool story.<br /> <br /> Edit: Page 10 of 2nd Edition Umbra: The Velvet Shadow is the part that specifies that Fera tend to turn into their respective ancestor spirits, as well as what happens to trapped mundanes. I've seen later publications generally hint at agreeing with this, but never seen the full splat on death/disconnection/starvation in the Umbra redone as fully hashed-out as the original block from 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hakaken &quot;the heart of fear&quot; was an ahroun shadow lord. What made him a totem was the wyrm itself. I believe he is one of 2 garou to completely traverse the black spiral to completion. His case is a bit different from getting disconnected. But similar to what I was thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}